---
/* The rate limiter, drawn and playable in one panel. Clients send requests to the API Gateway, which checks
   authentication and then asks the rate limiter, a separate service that holds the token bucket: "is quota available
   for this user?". Yes: the request goes on to the backend. No: the gateway answers 429 itself. The service names are
   generic, not product names. Tickets travel the diagram via limiter.js. */
---
<div class="dispenser card" id="dispenser">
  <figure class="arch">
    <div class="arch-map">
      <div class="arch-clients">
        <span class="arch-node">Clients</span>
      </div>
      <span class="arch-lane arch-in" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="arch-gateway">
        <span class="arch-label">API Gateway</span>
        <span class="arch-node">Authentication</span>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-quota">
        <p class="arch-ask"><span></span><span class="arch-lane" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Is quota available for this user?</span></p>
        <div class="arch-node hot">Rate limiter
          <div class="bucket" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="chip"></span><span class="chip"></span><span class="chip"></span><span class="chip"></span><span class="chip"></span>
          </div>
          <p class="bucket-label" id="bucket-label">5 of 5 tokens left</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <span class="arch-lane arch-go" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="arch-services">
        <span class="arch-label">Behind the gateway</span>
        <span class="arch-node">Backend services</span>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-parcels" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="arch-back"><span class="arch-lane arch-return" aria-hidden="true"></span>429 Too Many Requests: over the limit, answered at the gateway</p>
    <figcaption>Every request reaches the API Gateway, which checks authentication and then asks the rate limiter: is quota available for this user? If yes, the request goes on to the backend. If no, the gateway answers 429 Too Many Requests and the backend never sees it.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <ol class="tickets" id="tickets" aria-live="off"></ol>
  <p class="fallback" id="fallback">This demo needs JavaScript. It sends tickets through the rate limiter, which admits five and then answers 429 Too Many Requests until a new token arrives.</p>
</div>
<script>
  import '../../scripts/limiter.js';
</script>
